1. An OU is basically a container used to organize users and computers in Active Directory.

corp.example
│
├── IT
│   ├── PC001
│   ├── PC002
│   └── John
│
├── HR
│   ├── PC003
│   └── Sarah
│
└── Finance
    ├── PC004
    └── Ahmed

2. You can then say:

"Apply this GPO only to the Finance OU."

Therefore, the computers/users in Finance receive that policy.

3. Example: Password Policy

Suppose your company says:

Every domain user must have a password of at least 12 characters.

Instead of configuring every user individually, the administrator configures a policy.

Conceptually:

Password Policy
       |
       +-- Minimum password length = 12
       |
       +-- Password complexity = Enabled
       |
       +-- Password history = 10

For eg,

Ahmed
   ↓
Password must follow company policy

Sarah
   ↓
Password must follow company policy

John
   ↓
Password must follow company policy
